diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 4479b53..3e5592e 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -15,3 +15,30 @@ The application will now be running on `http://localhost:11224`.
 - **[React](https://react.dev/)**: Used for UI components.
 - **[Tailwind CSS](https://tailwindcss.com/)**: For styling the application.
 - **[Astro DB](https://docs.astro.build/en/guides/database/)**: Powers the comments feature, using a libSQL-compatible database.
+
+## Phone verification at sign-up
+
+Sign-up now sends an SMS with Twilio Verify and checks the code on the server before calling the existing registration API. Codes and provider credentials never enter client-side bundles. The challenge is bound to the username and server session, expires after 10 minutes, and allows five checks. Resends have a 30-second session cooldown. An approved challenge is retained until expiry if registration fails, allowing a retry without checking a consumed code again.
+
+Set these **server runtime** environment variables (do not prefix them with `PUBLIC_`):
+
+```text
+TWILIO_API_KEY=SK...
+TWILIO_API_SECRET=...
+TWILIO_VERIFY_SERVICE_SID=VA...
+TWILIO_VERIFY_TEMPLATE_SID=HJ...
+```
+
+Configure the Verify service for **six-digit codes** and select an approved custom SMS template whose final line binds the code to the deployed sign-up hostname. For example, an actual delivered SMS must look like:
+
+```text
+Your DevTools Times verification code is 012345.
+
+@your-deployed-hostname.example #012345
+```
+
+Use the actual hostname, without a scheme, port, or path, and no signature after that last line. Configure the template's code placeholder in Twilio; never hard-code the example code. See [Twilio verification templates](https://www.twilio.com/docs/verify/verification-templates). Automatic extraction requires HTTPS, browser support, user consent, and a matching SMS hostname. Keyboard autofill and manual entry remain available when WebOTP is unavailable or dismissed.
+
+Use persistent shared Astro session storage for multi-instance deployments. Configure Twilio Verify fraud protection, geographic permissions, and service rate limits before public use; session cooldowns alone do not prevent clients from creating new sessions. Without provider configuration the flow fails closed and cannot create an account.
+
+The existing external registration service is outside this repository. This app gates its registration request on phone verification and forwards the verified phone number, but the upstream service must enforce verification itself and store that phone number if verification must be mandatory for all API callers. The publicly accessible legacy registration endpoint cannot be secured by this client application alone.
